id: pm-rl-0x9x
title: Bound concurrent checkpoint fixture contention without losing promotions
description: "Investigate release CI checkpoint promotion lock conflict from GitHub issue #152; characterize loaded contention, preserve declared bounds and checkpoint roots, and prove any correction by behavioral revert."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#152"
created_at: "2026-11-07T15:24:16.420Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T16:06:29.183Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T15:25:02.608Z",codex-agent,"Read issue #152 and SDK issue #1516 including all comments. No synced match exists, so this item owns gh:unbraind/pm-rl#152. Baseline focused real-process checkpoint fixture passed 1/1 under existing host load. The shipped bounded-contention contract explicitly permits lock_conflict; the installed SDK exposes CommitWorkspaceTransactionOptions.lockWaitMs, so this is not a missing wait API. Next: 30 instrumented repetitions under one low-priority CPU burner, then deterministic live-holder timing and a behavioral revert proof. Full multi-hour npm/Bun release gates are delegated to CI by the task instruction."
  "2026-11-07T15:31:16.871Z",codex-agent,"Controlled live-holder reproduction failed 1/1 with the original 30000 ms fixture wait: a healthy parent holds sdk-workspace-transaction for 35000 ms; a waiting promoter reports lock_conflict/lock_owner_alive after 30007 ms (another waiter is serialized behind the approval preflight lock). This demonstrates an insufficient positive-fixture bound, not lock corruption or lost committed writes. Testing a fixture-only 120000 ms wait, aligned with its existing 120000 ms fit signal and inside its unchanged 900000 ms outer deadline. Production lock defaults, retry contracts, trainer budgets and pinned SDK remain unchanged. The unforced instrumented baseline remains at its original 30000 ms wait until all 30 repetitions finish."
  "2026-11-07T15:34:31.519Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable source copy, change only concurrentCheckpointPromotions waitMs default from 120000 to 30000 and run Node 26.13.0: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"outwait a healthy\" test/checkpoint-artifacts.test.ts. It fails 1/1 with SDK lock_conflict, lock_owner_alive, waited_ms=30006. The fixed 120000 ms implementation passed 1/1 on Node 24.19.0 and 1/1 on Node 26.13.0 before this revert; rerun the fixed test after all edits. Both promoters retain their original job identities, exactly one training charge each, both promoted roots and the single verified shared artifact. No SDK defect is established and no upstream issue should be filed."
  "2026-11-07T15:43:26.190Z",codex-agent,"Supplemental local health gate found a separate extension host version mismatch (pinned host 2026.11.3 versus automatically resolved pm-github host floor 2026.11.6); recorded with existing follow-up pm-rl-9uz4 instead of duplicating it. Tracker integrity and history drift checks pass. No history rewrite or dependency bump is part of this fix. The linked snapshot test command passes 2/2, including the fixed live-holder regression after the disposable revert proof."
  "2026-11-07T15:45:40.203Z",codex-agent,"Loaded baseline complete: 30/30 focused invocations pass, zero failures and zero lock_conflict reports, using Node 24.19.0, V8 test coverage, test-concurrency=2, and one low-priority CPU burner on the shared host. The original 30000 ms admission bound was retained throughout. This is an honest non-reproduction of the spontaneous hosted failure; the controlled 35000 ms live-holder case and revert proof demonstrate fixture scheduling sensitivity separately. The matching 30-run fixed-bound series has now started."
  "2026-11-07T15:47:53.419Z",codex-agent,"Final fixture behavioral revert repeated on Node 26.13.0: changing only PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS from 120000 back to 30000 in a disposable copy fails 1/1 with lock_conflict/lock_owner_alive, waited_ms=30085 on the approval lock queued behind the held workspace mutex. CI-style isolated health passes with only pre-existing advisories. Main advanced to release commit 25b4011; its authored runtime delta is only the version constant, and the branch fast-forwards to that release without changing dependency pins or checkpoint behavior."
  "2026-11-07T15:52:49.322Z",codex-agent,"Final source after the release fast-forward passes the linked snapshot command on Node 26.13.0: 2 tests, 2 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled/todo. This run follows the final literal-only behavioral revert and uses the fixed 120000 ms wait in both positive fixtures. The controlled case verifies the live holder lease remains byte-identical until release, original identities and exactly-once training charges, both promotion roots, and verified shared-artifact retention. No new pm CLI/SDK bug was established; the development health warning disappears under CI-style home isolation."
  "2026-11-07T16:06:26.978Z",codex-agent,"Final loaded result: before 0 failures / 30 runs; after 0 failures / 30 runs. All 60 instrumented Node 24.19.0 invocations pass without skip/cancel/todo or lock_conflict under one low-priority CPU burner, with test-concurrency=2. This does not reproduce or estimate the spontaneous hosted failure rate. Controlled final Node 26.13.0 sensitivity: original wait fails 1/1 after 30085 ms against a live owner; fixed wait passes 1/1, and the complete linked snapshot command passes 2/2 after the revert and release fast-forward. Classification (a): the positive fixture admission bound was below healthy instrumented contention; no pm-rl integrity defect or additional SDK defect is established. Build, typecheck, test compilation and lint pass; docstrings report 539 documented declarations across 62 sources, duplication is zero, and CI-style strict health passes with existing advisories. The 120000 ms fixture wait preserves existing fit/outer deadlines and all receipt, identity, accounting, root and artifact assertions. Full npm/Bun release gates are pending CI under the task instruction; no full coverage or release certification is claimed. See docs/checkpoint-contention.md. Ready for one PR fixing #152; leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
